/* Auto-generated from assets/background.png — see SPEC.md "Background asset" note. 
   Embedded as a data: URI (not loaded via <img src="assets/background.png">) so the export 
   canvas is never tainted: Chrome taints a canvas drawn from a separate file:// resource 
   load even in the same folder, which breaks canvas.toBlob() for both Copy PNG and 
   Export PNG. A data: URI has no separate origin, so this sidesteps the problem 
   entirely instead of working around it at export time. Classic script, no module, 
   so BACKGROUND_DATA_URL is just a global var — load this before app.js. */
var BACKGROUND_DATA_URL = "data:image/png;base64,";
